From 36bb46b90196e609bf0c319dfdef154e9b44f1d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 11:55:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00821/11171] [outer-loop] #3 in-loop energy-gate draft + #5 v2
 (deliverable features + waste trend)

#3 DRAFT (sudoku_inloop_energy_gate_v5_draft.py): the untested THIRD mode -
energy as a per-step FEASIBILITY GATE inside the decode loop (confidence-ordered,
prune the refiner's next-cell choice to the feasible set via the true scorer),
NOT descent and NOT rerank (both of which lost in v1-v4). Reuses v4's Refiner +
training. Falsification gate: gated > greedy by >=+0.03 on every seed. Compiles,
imports resolve, PEERS geometry verified. Ready for a paused-GPU window.

#5 v2: added deliverable-path features + per-quartile waste TREND. Findings:
 - deliv_hardware is the single biggest waster: 50.6% wasted, 1.57x base.
 - Waste TREND (early->recent quartiles): 18.6% -> 39.4% -> 41.2% -> 35.8%.
   Waste ROSE as the project added hardware/harness/cascade complexity and only
   modestly recovered; discipline rules slowed but did not reverse it to early
   levels. The dominant driver is structural (precondition/reachability failures),
   not planning -- so the highest-leverage fix is mechanical precondition gating of
   hardware/harness tasks BEFORE scheduling, not more planner-discipline prose.
 - Title/deliverable features keep holdout WASTED-AUROC ~0.57 (weak): a deployable
   meta-verifier needs live resource-state (board reachable? upstream harness READY?),
   i.e. a precondition oracle, not a text classifier. That is #5 v3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
